From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 13:28:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Scope shadow-tree stylesheets via per-root AuthorStyles

<style> elements inside a shadow tree now register with their root's
AuthorStyles (stylo's per-shadow cascade store) instead of the
document stylist; TShadowRoot::style_data hands the built CascadeData
to the rule collector, which already knows how to consult it (:host,
scoped rules, cascade order). Dirty roots are queued and their
CascadeData rebuilt at resolve_stylist; invalidation is a wholesale
host-subtree restyle at mutation time rather than plumbing
StylesheetInvalidationSet.

The subtle part is where a sheet was registered vs where its node
lives now: blitz processes <style> on every mutation that touches it
(maybe_record_node), so a detached style gets a document-stylist
registration first and a scoped one after insertion. Removal must
therefore target the recorded scope - nodes_to_stylesheet's value now
carries it - or the stale copy stays behind and leaks rules across
the boundary (and shadow-scoped entries must not serve as
insert-before anchors for the document stylist).

Also defuses the todo!() in implicit_scope_for_sheet_in_shadow_root:
returning None misdirects @scope inside shadow sheets (unimplementable
while OpaqueElement is a bare NodeId), vastly better than a panic.
